From 113529480194142eff5a1b2e9e7b8af8e22b10b5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Silicon Bakery <noreply@localhost>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 12:26:33 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] media: v4l2: add the P210 pixel format

P210 is the 4:2:2 counterpart of P010: a luma plane and a CbCr plane of
the same height, 10 bits per sample in the high bits of 16-bit little
endian words. DRM already has it (DRM_FORMAT_P210, 'P210'), FFmpeg calls
it AV_PIX_FMT_P210 and VA-API VA_FOURCC_P210; V4L2 had no name for it.

The Apple AVD decoder writes exactly this layout for 4:2:2 10-bit H.264
and HEVC and currently labels it P010, whose buffers are a third too
small for it. Use the same fourcc code as DRM.

This changes the uAPI header and v4l2-core, so it needs a kernel
rebuild; the out-of-tree AVD module only uses it when it is defined.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
